# Repo hygiene

Commit only what is required to clone, build, and run the app.

## Allowlist

- `app/src/` (main, test, androidTest)
- Gradle: `settings.gradle.kts`, `build.gradle.kts`, `app/build.gradle.kts`, `gradle.properties`, `gradle/libs.versions.toml`, `app/proguard-rules.pro`
- Wrapper: `gradlew`, `gradlew.bat`, `gradle/wrapper/`
- `.gitignore`, `.gitattributes`, `.cursor/rules/`

## Never commit

- `build/`, `.gradle/`, `.idea/`, `local.properties`
- `.cursor/skills/`, `.cursor/mcp.json`
- `*.apk`, `*.aab`, `*.jks`, `*.keystore`
- Loose files at repo root (`/*.png`, sketches, dumps)

## Agent duties

- Do not create files outside the allowlist unless the user explicitly asks (README, docs, samples, extra configs).
- Do not use `git add .` / `git add -A`. Add paths from the allowlist only.
- Before every commit, inspect `git status`. The index must contain only allowlisted files.

```text
# BAD
git add -A

# GOOD
git add app/src app/build.gradle.kts gradle .gitignore .cursor/rules
```
